<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian soybean and product market.</title>
<headline>Brazilian soybean and product market.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers reported the following Brazilian soybean, products basis levels.</p>
<p>(NS - no seller T-Trade P-Premium D-Discount, NB - no bidder)</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	  BASIS	  MONTH	   PREVIOUS*</p>
<p>Soybean (cents per bushel)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> June		20/18 D	June	    20/18 D</p>
<p> July		16/13 D	July	    16/13 D</p>
<p> August	    18/30 P	August	  18/30 P</p>
<p> Sept		15/35 P	Sept	    15/35 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	  BASIS	  MONTH	   PREVIOUS</p>
<p>Soymeal/Pellets (dollars per short tonne 48 pct profat)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> June		26/25 D	June	    26/25 D</p>
<p> July		26/25 D	July	    26/25 D</p>
<p> August	     10/8 D	August	   10/8 D</p>
<p> Sept		  6/3 D	Sept		6/3 D</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	 BASIS	   MONTH	  PREVIOUS</p>
<p>Soybean Oil (dollars per tonne, points per lb, crude, degummed)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> June		40/70 P	 June	   40/70 P</p>
<p> July		40/70 P	 July	   40/70 P</p>
<p> August	  even/50 P	 August     even/50 P</p>
<p> Sept	    even/50 P	 Sept	 even/50 P</p>
<p>NOTE: There will be no price message on Thursday 29 May as markets are closed for the Corpus Christi holiday. The next price message will be on Friday 30 May.</p>
</text>
